meta {
  name: List Apps
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/apps?status=published&page=1&page_size=20
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  status: published
  page: 1
  page_size: 20
  ~q:
}

docs {
  Anonymous-friendly catalogue list. Returns
  { items: [AppCard], total, page, page_size }. Each card carries the
  manifest fields (display_name, categories, risk_class, license) and
  chart_version of its published version.

  Filters:
    q           free-text LIKE search across slug, repo_owner, repo_name
    status      App.state filter (default: published)
    risk_class  filter by AI risk class: minimal | limited | high
                (reads from published version's appstore.yaml manifest)
    category    array-containment filter on spec.categories
                (e.g. "decision-support", "text-generation")
    page        1-based (default 1, max 1000)
    page_size   1..100 (default 20)

  Responses:
    200 OK   — paginated list; items may be empty on a fresh DB. deployed_in_my_org is true when the caller's org runs a live deployment of the app (always false for anonymous)
    422      — invalid query param shape (rare)

  To produce results: POST /api/v1/apps with a real GitHub repo, then
  approve via the audit decision flow.
}
